From: randallwang <randallwang@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] lir: a match/destructure `rest` alias is borrowed

A `(a & rest)` pattern binds `rest` to a BORROWED subview of the scrutinue:
the match decision tree loads it with the `Rest` intrinsic, which hands back a
cdr pointer into the scrutinee's region pages with NO owning reference. The
region solver registers a counted container read for call-site `rest()` /
`first()` only, never for pattern loads. Passing such an alias as an
owned-param call argument (tail or not) made the callee's owned-param release
free the caller's still-live scrutinee region — the match sibling of the
captured-upvalue tail-move-borrow UAF (`region-tail-move-borrow-uaf.lisp`).

Mark match/destructure-rest bindings borrowed: the lowerer tracks
`destructure_alias_bindings`, and `arg_leaf_is_borrowed` /
`tail_arg_is_borrowed` treat a call arg naming one as borrowed, minting a
fresh owning reference the callee's release balances. The scrutinee's own
reference is untouched.

Fixes the hypervisor's `graph:find-entry` over a `map`-built list (the
map-produced list's tail was freed and reused after a recursive match walk).

Regression: tests/elle/region-match-rest-tail-move-uaf.lisp.

